## Note: Math/ELA Scores Aren't on a Consistent Scale Across Years

The raw test score range shifts sharply starting in 2013 — this is a
change in the test/scoring scheme itself, not a change in student
performance, so raw scores from 2008-2012 and 2013-2017 aren't directly
comparable.

```{r score-range-table}
score_range_by_year |>
  knitr::kable(
    col.names = c("Year", "Min Math", "Max Math", "Min ELA", "Max ELA"),
    digits = 0
  )
```

**Takeaway:** because of this scale break, Visualizations 1 and 2 (which
use raw math/ELA scores) mix scores from both scoring regimes and
shouldn't be read as tracking a single continuous scale. Visualization 3
sidesteps this by using standardized (z-score) values computed within
each year, which puts every year on the same scale.

